{{!-- Save submits the form; Cancel is `type="button"`, so it cannot submit it by accident, and
      its handler only closes the window — nothing typed above has been written yet.

      Written out rather than looped over a `buttons` context: this footer has exactly these two
      buttons and it always will, and a literal `data-action` is the only kind
      `checks/actions-map.check.mjs` can pair with its handler.

      Neither carries `autofocus`: the caret belongs in the first field, not on a button, and two
      elements claiming it in one window is a race the browser resolves by source order.

      The rule over the buttons is the same drawn `hline` as the one under the tab strip, and it
      is inside this part's single root for the same reason the strip's is. --}}
<div class="cairn-edit-foot">
    <div class="cairn-edit-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="edit-foot-rule" data-ink-w="1.8"></div>
    <footer class="cairn-edit-footer">
        <button type="submit" class="cairn-edit-button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk" inert></i>
            <span>{{localize 'CAIRN.Edit.Save'}}</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="cairn-edit-button" data-action="cancel">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" inert></i>
            <span>{{localize 'CAIRN.Edit.Cancel'}}</span>
        </button>
    </footer>
</div>
